<s-1 id="RM00000224E000X_01_0002" proc-id="E0505_____000004P00000">
<ptxt>Inspect Crankshaft Oil Clearance</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Clean the main journals and bearings.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Align the claws and install the crankshaft bearings with oil grooves (upper bearings) to the cylinder block.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A053015J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Do not apply engine oil to the bearing installation surface or the back of the bearing.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Align the claws and install the crankshaft bearings No.2 (lower bearings) to the bearing caps.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A063909J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Do not apply engine oil to the bearing installation surface or the back of the bearing.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Place the crankshaft on the cylinder block.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Lay a strip of Plastigage across each crankshaft journal.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A087782J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Check the front marks of the bearing caps and install them to the cylinder block.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128241J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Apply a light coat of engine oil to the threads and seats of the bolts.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Tighten the crankshaft bearing cap bolts using the plastic region tightening method.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Temporarily tighten the bolts in 2-3 steps in the order shown in the illustration, then tighten them to the specified torque.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128235J02" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<torque>
<torqueitem>
<t-value1>20</t-value1>
<t-value2>204</t-value2>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Tighten the bolts again to the specified torque in the order shown in the illustration.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128235J02" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<torque>
<torqueitem>
<t-value1>40</t-value1>
<t-value2>408</t-value2>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Mark the front of the bolt heads with paint.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A051462J03" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Using the paint marks as a guide, tighten each bolt an additional 90° in the tightening order.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Check that all paint marks have been turned 90° in the tightening direction.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Do not turn the crankshaft during measurement.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Remove the bearing caps.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Measure the Plastigage at its widest point.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A129506J01" width="2.775699831in" height="5.787629434in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<subtitle>Standard</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>0.017-0.040mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
<subtitle>Limit</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>0.06mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten3>
<ptxt>After inspection, completely remove the Plastigage.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>If the clearance is more than the maximum, select and replace the bearings.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Add the cylinder block bore diameter mark and the crankshaft journal diameter mark, and determine the bearing size from the bearing selection mark.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>[Example] If the block bore diameter mark is "3" and the crankshaft journal diameter mark is "5", then 3+5 = 8, so select bearing selection mark "3".</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
