<s-1 id="RM00000224E000X_01_0006" proc-id="E0505_____000004T00000">
<ptxt>Install Oil Nozzle Sub-assembly NO.1</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a socket hexagon wrench (5mm), install the 4 oil nozzles No.1.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128251J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<torque>
<torqueitem>
<t-value1>7.0</t-value1>
<t-value2>71</t-value2>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224E000X_01_0007" proc-id="E0505_____000004U00000">
<ptxt>Install Piston</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a small screwdriver, install a new piston pin hole snap ring on one side only.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128244J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Install the snap ring with its end gap positioned as shown in the illustration.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Heat the piston to approximately 80°C.</ptxt>
<atten2>
<ptxt>The piston is hot, so always wear gloves when working.</ptxt>
</atten2>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Apply engine oil to the piston pin and the connecting rod small end.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Align the front mark of the piston with the front mark of the connecting rod, and push in the piston pin with your thumb until it contacts the snap ring.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128245J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Do not change the combination of the piston and piston pin.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a small screwdriver, install a new piston pin hole snap ring.</ptxt>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224E000X_01_0008" proc-id="E0505_____000004V00000">
<ptxt>Install Piston Ring Set</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Install the oil ring expander and oil ring by hand.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A131712J01" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Install the oil ring so that its end gap is on the opposite side from the expander end gap.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Securely install the expander into the inner groove of the oil ring.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a piston ring expander, install the rings so that the paint marks at the end gaps are on the right side.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128246J01" width="2.775699831in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Install the compression ring No.2 with the stamped mark (2N) facing upward.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Replacement compression rings No.1 and No.2 have no paint marks.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Position the piston ring end gaps as shown in the illustration.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128247J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224E000X_01_0009" proc-id="E0505_____000004W00000">
<ptxt>Install Crankshaft Bearing</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Align the claws and install the crankshaft bearings with oil grooves (upper bearings) to the cylinder block.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A053015J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Do not apply engine oil to the bearing installation surface of the cylinder block or the back of the bearing.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224E000X_01_0010" proc-id="E0505_____000004X00000">
<ptxt>Install Crankshaft Bearing NO.2</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Align the claws and install the crankshaft bearings No.2 (lower bearings) to the bearing caps.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A063909J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Do not apply engine oil to the bearing installation surface of the bearing cap or the back of the bearing.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224E000X_01_0011" proc-id="E0505_____000004Y00000">
<ptxt>Install Crankshaft Thrust Washer Upper</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Install the thrust washers to the No. No.3 journal of the cylinder block with the oil grooves facing outward.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A013501J02" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Be careful not to install the thrust washer set incorrectly.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Apply engine oil to the surfaces of the thrust washer set.</ptxt>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224E000X_01_0012" proc-id="E0505_____000004Z00000">
<ptxt>Install Crankshaft</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Apply engine oil to the upper bearing surfaces and install the crankshaft.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Apply engine oil to the lower bearing surfaces.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Check the front marks of the bearing caps and install them to the cylinder block.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128241J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Apply a light coat of engine oil to the threads and seats of the bolts.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Tighten the crankshaft bearing cap bolts using the plastic region tightening method.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Temporarily tighten the bolts in 2-3 steps in the order shown in the illustration, then tighten them to the specified torque.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128235J02" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<torque>
<torqueitem>
<t-value1>20</t-value1>
<t-value2>204</t-value2>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Tighten the bolts again to the specified torque in the order shown in the illustration.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128235J02" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<torque>
<torqueitem>
<t-value1>40</t-value1>
<t-value2>408</t-value2>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Mark the front of the bolt heads with paint.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A051462J03" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Using the paint marks as a guide, tighten each bolt an additional 90° in the tightening order.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Check that all paint marks have been turned 90° in the tightening direction.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Check that the crankshaft turns smoothly.</ptxt>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224E000X_01_0013" proc-id="E0505_____000005000000">
<ptxt>Install Connecting Rod Bearing</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Align the claws and install the connecting rod bearings to the connecting rods and connecting rod bearing caps.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128248J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Do not apply engine oil to the bearing installation surfaces of the connecting rods and caps or the back of the bearings.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224E000X_01_0014" proc-id="E0505_____000005100000">
<ptxt>Install Piston with Connecting Rod</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Apply engine oil to the cylinder walls, the piston circumference and the connecting rod bearing surfaces.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Check the positions of the piston ring end gaps again.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128247J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Check the front mark and, using a piston ring compressor, install the piston with connecting rod.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128249J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Keep the connecting rods and caps in the same combinations as before disassembly.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Check the combination of the connecting rod and cap and the front mark on the cap, and assemble the cap to the connecting rod.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A036691J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Apply a light coat of engine oil to the threads and seats of the bolts.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Tighten the connecting rod bolts using the plastic region tightening method.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a socket wrench (12mm), temporarily tighten the bolts in 2-3 steps, then tighten them to the specified torque.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A013397J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<torque>
<torqueitem>
<t-value1>25</t-value1>
<t-value2>250</t-value2>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Mark the front of the bolt heads with paint.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A101478J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Using the paint marks as a guide, tighten each bolt an additional 90°.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Check that the crankshaft turns smoothly.</ptxt>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
</subpara>
</para>
</ttl>
</section>
